WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.239 --> 00:00:01.399
(percussive jazz music)

00:00:01.399 --> 00:00:02.535
- [Voiceover] There's sun.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.087
There's sand.

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:05.254
There's speed.

00:00:06.198 --> 00:00:07.061
Well, hold on.

00:00:07.061 --> 00:00:08.514
I'm getting ahead of myself.

00:00:08.514 --> 00:00:09.730
(vintage music)

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:13.852
In 1947, 100 miles east of LA,
a bunch of World War II vets

00:00:13.852 --> 00:00:16.242
formed a car club called the Oilers,

00:00:16.242 --> 00:00:18.748
taking their Model T
Fords, hot-rodding them up

00:00:18.748 --> 00:00:21.306
and racing them in the Mojave desert.

00:00:21.306 --> 00:00:24.179
Eventually, the men got
old, the cars broke down,

00:00:24.179 --> 00:00:28.295
and their brand of bare-knuckle
drag racing all but stopped.

00:00:28.295 --> 00:00:29.355
Until now.

00:00:29.355 --> 00:00:32.688
(percussive jazz music)

00:00:34.779 --> 00:00:36.300
- My name is Mel Stultz.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.408
I'm with the Race of Gentlemen.

00:00:37.408 --> 00:00:38.624
My name's Bobby Green.

00:00:38.624 --> 00:00:40.392
I'm with the Race of Gentlemen.

00:00:40.392 --> 00:00:42.488
- [Voiceover] With the blessing
of the Oilers Club founders,

00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:44.456
Mel and Bobby resurrected the club,

00:00:44.456 --> 00:00:47.496
re-branding it the Race of Gentlemen.

00:00:47.496 --> 00:00:51.144
(upbeat jazz music)

00:00:51.144 --> 00:00:53.536
- What is the Race of Gentlemen?

00:00:53.536 --> 00:00:55.424
It’s a vintage car race on the beach,

00:00:55.424 --> 00:00:57.568
but there's that other layer to it.

00:00:57.568 --> 00:00:58.495
(engine revving)

00:00:58.495 --> 00:01:01.729
The Race of Gentlemen, in a
sense, is a time travel event.

00:01:01.729 --> 00:01:04.576
We go to great lengths to
make it feel like you could be

00:01:04.576 --> 00:01:06.600
in a different time era.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.618
- [Voiceover] And the
rules of the race stay true

00:01:07.618 --> 00:01:09.550
to the time period, as well.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:13.182
The body, engine and running
gear must be of a certain age

00:01:13.182 --> 00:01:15.262
and must be American-made.

00:01:15.262 --> 00:01:17.903
- Well, there's definitely
something about American cars.

00:01:17.903 --> 00:01:21.719
All those incredible cars that we created

00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:24.390
starting from, let's say the 1910s

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:28.110
up until probably about
the 60s were so different

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.950
than anywhere else in the world.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.143
Things today are made to last a month.

00:01:32.143 --> 00:01:35.310
The 1932 Ford is made to last forever.

00:01:36.766 --> 00:01:38.679
- It's not just about
the car and the bikes.

00:01:38.679 --> 00:01:42.303
It's about the camaraderie
and all the things that go in.

00:01:42.303 --> 00:01:43.710
People are like oh, this is so cool

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.030
because not only is it a
race, it's like a scene,

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.046
it's like a set.

00:01:47.046 --> 00:01:48.670
It's lost in time.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:49.911
- [Voiceover] And for
the Race of Gentlemen,

00:01:49.911 --> 00:01:53.367
the love of classic American
cars transcends generations.

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:54.853
- [Mel] You've got young kids

00:01:54.853 --> 00:01:57.429
that want to have a more simple life

00:01:57.429 --> 00:01:59.309
and build and make things,

00:01:59.309 --> 00:02:01.694
and them you've got the old generation.

00:02:01.694 --> 00:02:03.923
We all kind of celebrate that time

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:06.549
when we built and we did
things with our hands.

00:02:06.549 --> 00:02:07.525
(motor humming)

00:02:07.525 --> 00:02:09.445
- [Bobby] The Race of
Gentlemen is definitely helping

00:02:09.445 --> 00:02:12.653
to keep this sport alive
with a new generation.

00:02:12.653 --> 00:02:15.653
(upbeat jazz music)

